      C: `Choice C is incorrect. It proposes policy solutions (legal mandates and bans) rather than making a thesis claim about what kind of problem resistance is. A thesis sentence should advance an analytical argument; this choice makes only prescriptive recommendations, which belong in a different section of the essay.`,
      D: `Choice D is incorrect. It draws on only the fourth note and partially undermines the framing (by implying the crisis may be less intractable than claimed), which contradicts rather than supports the student's argument about the severity and structural nature of the economic problem.`,
